<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> No</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror, Emotional, Comedy, Mystery</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Standard</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An SCP entry about an anomalous SCP entry.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Out of nowhere, a new fully authorized SCP entry has appeared randomly in the Foundation's database, where it describes an entity so foreign and alien to the current local reality, where any and all sophisticated informational stimuli regarding it cannot be transcribed and comprehended when unaided, resulting in the immediate loss of said information after it removes its presence, such as memory. Translations, however, are perfectly comprehensible, such as written or recorded materials. However, it may also be corrupted if said entity acts upon it. The entity refers to itself in the English language as &quot;Your Warden&quot; or &quot;Them&quot;, a being that proclaimed itself as the safe keeper of all reality from itself, by destroying realities beyond repair, and cleaning those near broken. However, even with all the SCP shenanigans, the time it spent observing the world(s) in this local reality had changed its mind, and coming to the absurd conclusion that the SCP universe may be the most convoluted, but it is far from broken, and everything belongs, resulting in its departure leaving this reality to its own business.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The mass confusion where absolutely no one remembers anything regarding the Security Containment Procedure ever transpiring adds to the curiosity of the reader, and it also enjoys the treatment of a drastic mood change, it slowly shifts from being a lighthearted slice of life reality hopping Mary Sue into a dreadful, cosmic horror-esque atmosphere. The horror will be mostly informational horror, the feeling of dread when presented absurd consensuses and information. There's just too much out there, and you have no say over it. The struggle to understand will lead to hatred, fear, confusion, denial, and much more will be explored.</p>

							</div>

								
					
