<p>Greetings there, fellow SCP enthusiasts!</p>
<p>I am Seereeni (Seh-re-nii), and after roughly 5 years of knowing about and following the SCP universe, I decided to make an account of my own, and contribute to this wonderful place in whatever way I can.</p>
<p>One of mine own desires is to write an SCP, humanoid at that, which can then by used by everyone here, veteran and newbie, to link together all the SCPs, in one way or another, either for tales, to create new SCPs, to write interesting logs, or to explain something which they find hard to explain.</p>
<p>Hard? Oh yes, that's how a challenge should be.</p>
<p>I am also a writer on Fanfiction, as as far as my readers have commented, I am apparently almost typo-free in my writing. Do you have a tale or SCP you wish someone to look over for typos? Then do contact me, I am more than happy to help.</p>
<p>Lastly, as you have probably noticed, I am very&#8230;detailed in my explanations. This is, naturally, a good thing for a writer, but less so for an SCP Foundation member, something I am very much aware of. I have read the rules and I know that an SCP page should be professional and not use more words than needed. I will try my best to abide by these rules.</p>
<p>With that said, I still have a hard time understanding how this site works. So many links directing one to other links, then to other links&#8230;sigh. I barely know how Discord works.</p>
<p>Thus, to all of you veterans who have taken it upon themselves to answer newbie questions&#8230;.I pity you, and I am sorry. I'll try to learn fast and keep your suffering minimal.</p>
<p>Kay bye.</p>

